{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/91722-first-impressions-and-computations-from-playing-dtd","id":91722,"title":"First impressions and computations from playing DtD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-15T10:31:13-07:00","id":91722,"title":"First impressions and computations from playing DtD","content":"So I've played my first session of DtD today and it went generally very well. My players loved the world and really engaged with the idea of the Cover and hiding from the GM.<br /> <br /> However, a few things played completely differently from how I expected and I am not sure if I did something wrong as a storyteller or if it's fine but my initial intuition was wrong.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the players were a bit disappointed that they didn't get to use many exciting powers. The various Embeds that they had weren't directly relevant most of the time. Their Demon forms were much more useful but they were very afraid to use them. Not because of Compromise Rolls but because of Aether. They viewed Aether as a very scarce resource, which is not the impression I got from the rules but they do have a point.<br /> <br /> The story starts very early in their existence as demons, directly after their fall. So they haven't discovered any infrastructure or gadgets yet, and haven't met any other demons or angels yet. So the only way to get Aether is by adopting the Demonic Form. Now they didn't mind an occasional compromise roll but the thing is it's pretty pointless. At Primum 1 you are only going to get 1 Aether this way. But then you need to spend 1 Aether to revert to Cover. So net gain of zero. And of course they don't have any other covers to Go Loud (and at Primum 1 can't even get them). So yeah, I couldn't really provide good reasons for them not to hoard Aether and hence they avoided using Demonic Forms and Aetheric Resonance.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it seems to me that partial demonic transformations with high cover is just a Beat cow. What one of my players did (and she is not at all a power gamer, it just made sense to her because she was trying to save on Aether) was to manifest one Demonic Power and then simply always keep it on. It was a rivet arm so it was relatively easy to hide with long sleeves, gloves etc. Now she had 3 Wits and 4 Manipulation. So the compromise roll was 7+1(Cover Bonus)+6(unmanifested forms). Which naturally gave her an Exceptional Success and a Beat. But because she just kept it, every scene we did a new compromise roll with a cumulative -1 penalty. And while, yes, the dice pool was slowly getting lower, she did star with 14 dice originally so she just kept getting exceptional successes and Beats scene after scene. I am not sure that's how it was meant to work though. Especially since the other player didn't have any easily hide-able Demonic Forms and so quite quickly got behind on Beats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T13:49:25-07:00","id":91835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The story starts very early in their existence as demons, directly after their fall. So they haven't discovered any infrastructure or gadgets yet, and haven't met any other demons or angels yet. So the only way to get Aether is by adopting the Demonic Form. Now they didn't mind an occasional compromise roll but the thing is it's pretty pointless. At Primum 1 you are only going to get 1 Aether this way. But then you need to spend 1 Aether to revert to Cover. So net gain of zero. And of course they don't have any other covers to Go Loud (and at Primum 1 can't even get them). So yeah, I couldn't really provide good reasons for them not to hoard Aether and hence they avoided using Demonic Forms and Aetheric Resonance. </div> </div> </div> Ah, this is the delicious irony of playing Demon. The only way they can actually get power (ie aether) is by interacting with God and the Angels in someway. They need to chase after what they just left in order to survive. They're almost parasites, living off the angelic like that.<br /> <br /> Despite having decided to Fall, they still need God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, it seems to me that partial demonic transformations with high cover is just a Beat cow. What one of my players did (and she is not at all a power gamer, it just made sense to her because she was trying to save on Aether) was to manifest one Demonic Power and then simply always keep it on. It was a rivet arm so it was relatively easy to hide with long sleeves, gloves etc. Now she had 3 Wits and 4 Manipulation. So the compromise roll was 7+1(Cover Bonus)+6(unmanifested forms). Which naturally gave her an Exceptional Success and a Beat. But because she just kept it, every scene we did a new compromise roll with a cumulative -1 penalty. And while, yes, the dice pool was slowly getting lower, she did star with 14 dice originally so she just kept getting exceptional successes and Beats scene after scene. I am not sure that's how it was meant to work though. Especially since the other player didn't have any easily hide-able Demonic Forms and so quite quickly got behind on Beats. </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I think that's a potential rule loophole they missed. I've run into the same problem - high covers prompting rolls tend to generate beats and push your Cover even higher, which gives you more beats, which etc.<br /> <br /> Another thing to watch out for is a few of the Embeds that prompt Compromise rolls; they can be exceedingly overpowered. There's one that lets you change consequences at whim. Up to several minutes worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-16-2014, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T02:01:57-07:00","id":92185,"title":"","content":"As a storyteller it is well within your right to refuse Beats because the conditions posed no actual risk. Beats are there to reward positive interaction with the story, not exploitation of the system. Either way, a little Golden Ruling will patch it right up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T03:34:52-07:00","id":92721,"title":"","content":"Fair enough about the Golden Rule. But usually, if one is playing according to RAW, Golden Rulling is usually applied to situations away from the &quot;mean&quot;. But this is the hard core of one of the poster mechanics. Under *any* circumstances the absolute minimum that a starting demon will roll when partially transforming into one demonic form is 10 dice. So the absolute absolute minimum dice pool on average produces more than 3 successes. You don't need to be a power gamer or come up with unlikely scenarios to be in the realm of guaranteed exceptional successes. And if Aether is available you don't even need to sustain cumulative penalty rolls; just keep reactivating the demonic power anew.<br /> <br /> But yes, ST adjudication will help of course. It's just Demon is already pretty heavy on ST management and it's strange that this is not a situation where alternatives have been considered. It just leads to feel-bad with players. It's one thing when they are not expecting a Beat but you want to reward them for good role-playing and another when they are completely expecting a Beat and you have to put them down on the grounds of not-enough-risk-taking even though their play was perfectly legitimate from the RP point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T09:36:58-07:00","id":92839,"title":"","content":"I'm not suggesting you blindside them with it, talk to your players and let them know it's clearly exploiting the rules, so you're changing it. Alternatively just stop making them roll every scene. A roll with next to no chance of failure just slows down play anyway. Reserve the rolls for when exposure actually poses a risk in play, I'll bet they stop doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-17-2014, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T09:51:56-07:00","id":92844,"title":"","content":"I've been running Demon since the week the Kickstarter started and have found it to be complete opposite, my players almost never end up needing Aether at all. Some of them do partial transformations multiple times per scene, and you are definitely right about the compromise roll being trivial to exceptionally succeed on. But we don't like the beats system anyway, we give out an equal number of beats or xp at the end of every game so that everyone is fairly rewarded rather then Min Maxers getting tons of extra beats for risk free partial transformations.<br /> <br /> But Aether is really easy to get once a Demon has even a little experience with their city. Demon's can recognize infrastructure when they see it, so a quick drive around the city will probably show them a lot of possible targets for getting Aether. Getting Aether from infrastructure is risky, but while all infrastructure provides an equal amount of Aether, not all infrastructure is equally important and protected. For example in How an Angel dies in the back of the book, the Infrastructure is a main bridge so any demon driving over it would recognize it, and it isn't guarded and nothing is done to the stigmatic that breaks the linchpin every day.<br /> <br /> Also, as people start getting their Cipher done and Primum goes up, they can easily refill some by switching to Demon form. And if they hit 0 in Demon form, they will always gain more. Even with Primum 1 it is possible to get a 10 and reroll, so even with 1 Primum they can keep spending that last Aether until they get 2 and will be able to still have 1 after spending to switch out of demon form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T09:57:30-07:00","id":92847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just leads to feel-bad with players. It's one thing when they are not expecting a Beat but you want to reward them for good role-playing and another when they are completely expecting a Beat and you have to put them down on the grounds of not-enough-risk-taking even though their play was perfectly legitimate from the RP point of view. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially since the other player didn't have any easily hide-able Demonic Forms and so quite quickly got behind on Beats. </div> </div> </div>It seems to me like the current (RAW) system that you are using is leading to feel-bad with the rest of the players in the group who don't happen to have Forms that they can just wear a jacket and gloves to cover up, though, and I find that more of a problem than not giving a Beat to someone who is *literally* just continuing to do the same thing scene after scene for no apparent reason other than being able to. (After all, the primary purpose of the Beat system is to encourage players to help drive the story by role-playing their characters). As it stands, though, I would probably just have a discussion with my players before the next session (either individually or as a group) to see how much of a problem the *other* players have with Beatfest2014, then limit the Beats per session accordingly. (My gut would be 1 Beat per session unless the player can actually describe to you how they &quot;incorporate(d) it into their Cover&quot; on any Exceptional Success in later scenes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not suggesting you blindside them with it, talk to your players and let them know It's clearly exploiting the rules, so your changing it. Alternatively just stop making them roll every scene. A roll with next to no chance of failure just slows down play anyway. Reserve the rolls for when exposure actually poses a risk in play, I'll bet they stop doing it. </div> </div> </div>(This was posted after I started replying). This actually seems like a &quot;cleaner&quot; way of limiting Beats from Compromise rolls.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2495-rumanchu","name":"rumanchu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T10:36:46-07:00","id":92863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hulsmanm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/91722-first-impressions-and-computations-from-playing-dtd?p=92844#post92844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been running Demon since the week the Kickstarter started and have found it to be complete opposite, my players almost never end up needing Aether at all.<br /> [...]<br /> But Aether is really easy to get once a Demon has even a little experience with their city. Demon's can recognize infrastructure when they see it, so a quick drive around the city will probably show them a lot of possible targets for getting Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, how do you and your players treat Aetheric Resonance in respect of getting Aether out of Infrastructure? Is it the case that because they know infrastructure on sight and because they know infrastructure provides Aether, they just kind of &quot;do&quot; it, without needing to scout out with Aetheric Resonance first?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, all very good comments, all of you, thank you! One thing i was considering was using group beats for the &quot;purely mechanical&quot; beats (e.g. from &quot;safe&quot; compromise rolls or conditions) and reserve individual beats for driving the story forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T10:46:09-07:00","id":92866,"title":"","content":"One of the characters started with Like I Built It and that doesn't require Aether to use. So its never been an issue trying to find the point that they can plug in to get Aether. Without that Embed it probably could take a long time investigating physically to find the plug in point, but Aetheric Resonance would definitely speed it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T14:47:41-07:00","id":92983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/91722-first-impressions-and-computations-from-playing-dtd?p=92863#post92863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, how do you and your players treat Aetheric Resonance in respect of getting Aether out of Infrastructure? Is it the case that because they know infrastructure on sight and because they know infrastructure provides Aether, they just kind of &quot;do&quot; it, without needing to scout out with Aetheric Resonance first?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, all very good comments, all of you, thank you! One thing i was considering was using group beats for the &quot;purely mechanical&quot; beats (e.g. from &quot;safe&quot; compromise rolls or conditions) and reserve individual beats for driving the story forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that as former angels, demons have a good understanding of how infrastructure would be laid out. Not really specific blue prints, per se but like a general idea, (i.e. fridges and stoves in kitchens.. generally). which would help them find a spot to plug in. I'm also of the opinion that it wouldn't be too difficult for demon's to find a way to get some aether out of infrastructure as it's a by-product and considered waste,,<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T07:07:34-07:00","id":93468,"title":"","content":"I personally call either for a Resonance roll, or an Investigation/Science/Occult roll to figure it out. A lot like jacking in, you're actively trying to hack into a system. So, you'd need to either have some kind of detector (resonance roll), or study the layout and figure out where the waste output would be (the skill roll). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T11:41:36-07:00","id":95809,"title":"","content":"Do you mean a Resistance roll? Or Aetheric Resonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T04:53:57-07:00","id":96276,"title":"","content":"Aetheric Resonance. Think of the resonance as a Geiger counter - using a tool to detect the aether &quot;radiation.&quot; Or, you could use your knowledge of a structure to figure out the most likely place that the waste unit would be venting radiation, and using logical deduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}